WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-ID

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.859
Hi, welcome back to Lam Rim.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.080
We start with episode number 9.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.320
I like to call it
"A Visit to the Middle of the Sun".

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.900
We've been talking about
something big and pretty powerful--

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:29.380
like a nuclear bomb used to clean ketchup
off your clothes or something.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.879
And I'm not exaggerating.
I want you to think like that.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.410
Imagine--

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.240
so today in America, it's Independence Day.
I'm talking about Independence Day.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:53.600
Often we go on picnics with family.
It's the middle of summer.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:02.880
And American kids will eat a hot dog
or a hamburger and they'll add too much ketchup,
and a little drop of ketchup will fall here.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:13.200
Imagine that to clean it, mom sent a shirt or blouse to the middle of the sun

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.420
...

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.840
to clean a little tomato sauce, red ketchup.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.380
I know it sounds like a strange image,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.020
but I want you to try to think about it.
I want you to try to think about that.

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.060
I don't know what can compare it.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.980
Yeah, I don't know.
Put a small object in the middle of the sun, okay?

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.120
So we're going to visit the middle of the sun today.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:55.280
And I'm happy to announce that we've just reached the third and final section of the lam rim.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.360
Steps to enlightenment.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.700
As now we will enter
into the activities of bodhisattvas.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:12.040
We will go into the way of
thinking and acting like a bodhisattva,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.260
which is the highest capacity.
kyebu chenpo (KYES BU CHEN PO)

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.700
Which means a person with great capacity.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.280
For those of you, especially those who have been following this lam rim for the past ten years,

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.860
you should be super happy that you survived
and I survived to the end.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.580
We are at the final part.
This is the third and final part.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.360
Well, the mathematicians among you should be thinking, Geshe-la,

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.529
you said there's 25% left.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.240
So why is this the third and final part?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:03:02.500
And the answer is that the treatment
by Pabongka Rinpoche on the last two days of
lam rim was too short.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:09.540
His presentation on meditation
and seeing emptiness, the

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.480
last two of the six perfections, is
not very long.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.680
And I don't know what happened.
I mean, sometimes--

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.820
it's like the sponsor comes to him and says we're going to run out of food in two days.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.860
Finish it!

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:31.140
Maybe--
maybe this is a mystical message from Tara.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.960
Maybe, I don't know,
maybe he has an appointment in another city.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:50.480
But if you ask me, Pabongka Rinpoche
made the last two sections shorter because
Je Tsongkhapa already covered everything in his big Lam Rim.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.600
"The Great Book of
Steps on the Path to Enlightenment,"
Lam Rim Chenmo

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:01.040
Tsongkapa did such a great job that I think,
I can see Pabongka Rinpoche saying,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.540
you know,
there's not much reason for me to teach this section

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:12.560
because Tsongkhapa already taught it,
and he's wonderful.

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.940
There are many stories about
Tsongkhapa writing those last two sections

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.780
and I'm very happy
that we're going to do it together.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:29.260
So we're going to finish this lam rim series
with these wonderful teachings on meditation and emptiness.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:38.680
So that's why the section on the steps on the path for people who have bodhichitta,

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.440
for Bodhisattvas, is

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.020
not as long as it should be.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.640
So here we come in.
Let's read the Tibetan text.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.780
sumpa kyebu chenpoy lam gyi rim (GSUM PA SKYES BU CHEN PO'I LAM GYI RIM)
par lo jang wa la (PAR BLO SBYANG BA LA) Let

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:57.820
's train our hearts in the steps on the path
for people with great capacity.

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.520
People who are  Bodhisattva.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.700
thek chen gyi juk go sem kyed kho nar ten pa phen yun dang cey pa (THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS BSKYED KHO NAR BSTAN PA PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA)

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.500
He said we will cover
this bodhisattva way of life,

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.560
we will cover it in three different steps.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.440
Number one.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.860
thek chen gyi jug go (THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO)
If you want to enter the bodhisattva path,
there is only one way to get there.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.620
And that is by achieving a certain state of mind.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:29.660
If you want to gain enlightenment,
if you want to have the opportunity to gain enlightenment,

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.260
if you want to have the opportunity to help the world, there is
only one way.
You must have bodhichitta.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:44.460
You must have the desire to attain enlightenment
in order to be able to help countless beings.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.700
Now, I want to talk about something that is countless.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.500
Bodhichitta is aimed at countless sentient beings.

00:05:53.500 --> 00:06:00.540
It is not aimed at everyone in your city or everyone in your country or all  people on this planet.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.920
Zoom in--

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.800
if we want to send a virus to the center of the sun,
if we want to visit the center of the sun,

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:14.220
get out of the idea that we're working
for everyone on this planet.
No. Get out

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:23.680
of the idea that we're trying to help
all the fish and all the birds and all the animals
that walk on dry land.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.840
No.

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.620
That's not the point.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.560
We're encompassing the entire universe.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:39.300
We decided today that I want to help
every living being in the universe.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.540
Every little virus.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.360
Bacteria.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.300
Every whale.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.640
Every human being in the universe.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:58.980
So go out at night in Sedona, or outside of Sedona--
Rim Rock is better.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:03.340
And look at the stars and try to imagine.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:20.640
So first, you can't practice the bodhisattva way of life
if you don't expand your mind for it, for that purpose.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.709
And if you actually experience it,
which takes some practice,

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:30.850
if you actually send your mind--

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:41.480
if you can actually get bodhichitta,
then the things you have to do in this world are nothing.

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.780
Nothing. Meaningless.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:51.380
To help everyone in this world, that's not  nothing.
Easy.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.640
phen yun dang cey pa (PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA) means
I want to tell you the benefits of thinking like that.
That's the first step.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.657
jang chub tu sem kyed pay tsul (BYANG CHUB TU SEMS BSKYED PA'I TSUL) The
second step.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.560
How do you get this breakthrough?
Mental Breakthrough?

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.180
How do you see the whole universe
and all beings in it?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.800
And then develop love for them.
Is that possible?

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.760
Is that possible?
That's the second step. The

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.560
third step.
semkye nay chud pa la lob tsul lo (SEMS BSKYED NAS SPYOD PA LA SLOB TSUL LO)

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:27.080
We will learn how to behave like a bodhisattva.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:34.900
Once you have the wish to become a bodhisattva
then what to do?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:41.300
How do I use my time and day
if I want to behave like a bodhisattva?

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.260
What should I do?

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.600
What is my schedule plan?

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.200
Okay. This is the first one.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:58.860
dang po ni (DANG PO NI,)
de tar kye bu chung  dring gi kab su ngenjung gi sam pay kun nay lang (DE LTAR SKYES BU CHUNG 'BRING GI SKABS SU NGES 'BYUNG GI BSAM PAS KUN NAS BSLANGS)

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:08.340
So now that we have gone through the steps for people with lower and middle capacities,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.960
at least you should have a feeling that

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.100
this life really is pain, this life really is trouble.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.580
The virus just makes it obvious.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.020
But it has always been like that. There has

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.940
always been a virus called death.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.280
This virus is a new one. It is much smaller.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.340
But at least now we all think about it.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.220
hlak pay lab pa sum la bed pay (LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM LA 'BAD PAS)

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.479
We should
work on three wonderful trainings.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.580
Treating others well.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.720
Taking time for meditation.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:52.980
And then try to see
that things do not come from their own side.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:59.540
bed pay rang cig pu ('BAD PAS RANG GCIG PUS)
thar way go phang (THAR BA'I  GO 'PHANG)
thob tzam dang khor wa (THOB TZAM DANG 'KHOR BA)
len dok tzam jung (LAS LDOG TZAM 'BYUNG)

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.960
You can achieve nirvana on your own

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.980
and you can step off the Wheel of Life.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:11.500
If you practice those postures as far as you can, it's possible.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.000
We've taught you, we're done with it.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
de tzam gyi mi chok (DE TZAM GYIS MI CHOG)

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.347
But I don't want you to stop

00:10:18.347 --> 00:10:20.880
there. I don't want you to stop there. I want you--

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.040
there are bigger fish to fry.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:30.980
There are much bigger fish to fry. Don't stop there.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.680
pang ja tham ced ma pang (SPANG BYA THAMS CAD MA SPANGS)

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.500
If you only follow what I've taught you so far,

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.260
you won't cleanse your heart

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.560
of all the dirty things there.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.240
thob ja yun ten (THOB BYA YON TAN)
tham ced kyang yong su ma dzok pay (THAMS  CAD KYANG YONGS SU MA RDZOGS PAS)

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.560
And you haven't achieved

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.120
all the highest spiritual qualities
that you can achieve.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.680
ma dzok pay (MA RDZOGS PAS)
Therefore

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:02.480
rang dun dang (RANG DON DANG,)
shen dun yang nyi tse wa lay min jung (GZHAN DON YANG NYI TSE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG)

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:08.320
nyi tse wa (NYI TSE BA) that's a very disappointing word here.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.600
It's a very sad word here.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:16.340
It says you can work on the path that I've taught you so far,

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.480
you can do
all the meditations that I've taught you so far,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:25.120
but the good that
you'll do for yourself and for others

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.040
is just a tiny fraction of what you need to do.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.900
(NYI TSE BA) means it's just a tiny fraction
of what you need to do.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:43.520
And by the way, the common usage of that word is the Tibetan word for hell on earth.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.900
Which is very strange.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.580
So there's a big hell that people go to.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:56.840
But I always think of people who have car accidents and their cars explode and catch fire.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.945
In  The ancient scripture is called
nyi tsi way nyal wa (NYI TSI BA'I DMYAL BA).

00:12:02.945 --> 00:12:08.220
A small hell in this place. In this real world.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.080
And this word nyi tsi wa means just a small piece.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:17.780
And it says here, you want to help yourself
and you want to help others.

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.420
All I've been teaching you for 10 years is...
nyi tsi wa.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:30.160
This is just a small part of what you can do, and now we're ready to start the serious stuff.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:35.880
Now, Geshe-la, why did we spend 10 years doing nyi tsi wa, the small things?

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.460
Why don't we just go straight to the higher things?

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:44.660
Because the small things are the ladder
that helps you reach the higher things.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:50.080
You can't reach the higher things
unless you do the other two parts.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:55.093
Unless you practice all the steps in the lam rim
in the right order,

00:12:55.093 --> 00:12:58.460
you'll never get to the bodhisattva part.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.560
So, you can't say I don't want it.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:10.260
Part of the bodhisattva way of life is mastering the lower paths that help you get there.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.760
And you never refuse.  them.
You just grow from there.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:21.140
mi jung shing lar thek chen (MI 'BYUNG ZHING SLAR THEG CHEN)
la shi nay juk gu la (LA GZHI NAS 'JUG DGOS LA)

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.320
This is an idea in Buddhism,

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.320
that as soon as you are ready,

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.460
and as soon as you have the preparation,

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.300
you should jump right into the
bodhisattva way of life

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.080
because otherwise--
you will have to do it again,

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.749
sooner or later, you have to get here.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.700
Maybe during this lifetime.
Maybe in the next lifetime.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:57.780
People come to me from time to time and say I'm going to take a break from this dharma.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.960
I feel like I need a break.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:05.740
I have other things to do now.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.600
I have a big project at work.
or I have family problems right now

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.600
and I need a break.

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.400
I told one of my teachers once when I was in India, I remember

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.350
45 years ago.

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:31.960
And I said, "I have to take a break," and they looked at me and said, "Yeah, okay, but you'll come back."

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.120
You'll come back because there's nowhere else to go.

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:44.300
You'll come back. You'll come back because you have to come back here.  Life will bring you back here.

00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:47.929
Because that's life. You need the lam rim.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.901
Life will always bring you back to the lam rim.
Unless you die.

00:14:52.901 --> 00:14:55.680
And it will still bring you back there later.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.600
lar (SLAR) means you have to come back again.
lar thek chen la shi nay (SLAR THEG CHEN LA GZHI NAS)

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:07.250
shi nay (GZHI NAS) means you'll waste a lot of time
if you have to come back there.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:12.780
You might as well finish it now
instead of coming back later. The

